    modelAnswer: "1. Let the two cells have terminal potential difference V across common terminals A and B. Current I = I1 + I2.\n2. For first cell: V = E1 - I1 \xB7 r1 => I1 = (E1 - V) / r1.\n3. For second cell: V = E2 - I2 \xB7 r2 => I2 = (E2 - V) / r2.\n4. Total current: I = (E1 - V) / r1 + (E2 - V) / r2 = (E1 / r1 + E2 / r2) - V \xB7 (1 / r1 + 1 / r2).\n5. Rearranging for V:\nV \xB7 [ (r1 + r2) / (r1 \xB7 r2) ] = [ (E1 \xB7 r2 + E2 \xB7 r1) / (r1 \xB7 r2) ] - I\nV = [ (E1 \xB7 r2 + E2 \xB7 r1) / (r1 + r2) ] - I \xB7 [ (r1 \xB7 r2) / (r1 + r2) ].\n6. Comparing with V = E_eq - I \xB7 r_eq:\nE_eq = (E1 \xB7 r2 + E2 \xB7 r1) / (r1 + r2), and 1 / r_eq = 1 / r1 + 1 / r2 => r_eq = (r1 \xB7 r2) / (r1 + r2).",
