    questionType: "LA",
    questionText: "An insurance company insured 2000 scooter drivers, 4000 car drivers and 6000 truck drivers. The probability of an accident is 0.01, 0.03 and 0.15 respectively for scooter, car and truck drivers. One of the insured persons meets with an accident. What is the probability that he is a scooter driver?",
    stepRubrics: [
      { step: "Define partition events E1, E2, E3 and accident event A", marks: 0.5 },
      { step: "Calculate prior probabilities: P(E1) = 2/12 = 1/6, P(E2) = 4/12 = 1/3, P(E3) = 6/12 = 1/2", marks: 1 },
      { step: "State conditional probabilities: P(A|E1) = 0.01, P(A|E2) = 0.03, P(A|E3) = 0.15", marks: 0.5 },
      { step: "State Bayes\u2019 theorem formula for P(E1|A)", marks: 1 },
      { step: "Calculate denominator and obtain final fraction: 1 / 52", marks: 2 }
    ],
    modelAnswer: "1. Definition of Events:\nLet E1 = Event that insured person is a scooter driver.\nLet E2 = Event that insured person is a car driver.\nLet E3 = Event that insured person is a truck driver.\nLet A = Event that insured person meets with an accident.\n\n2. Prior Probabilities (Total drivers = 2000 + 4000 + 6000 = 12000):\nP(E1) = 2000 / 12000 = 1 / 6\nP(E2) = 4000 / 12000 = 2 / 6 = 1 / 3\nP(E3) = 6000 / 12000 = 3 / 6 = 1 / 2.\n\n3. Conditional Probabilities:\nP(A | E1) = 0.01 = 1 / 100\nP(A | E2) = 0.03 = 3 / 100\nP(A | E3) = 0.15 = 15 / 100.\n\n4. By Bayes\u2019 Theorem:\nP(E1 | A) = [ P(E1) \xB7 P(A | E1) ] / [ P(E1) \xB7 P(A|E1) + P(E2) \xB7 P(A|E2) + P(E3) \xB7 P(A|E3) ]\n\nNumerator:\n(1 / 6) \xB7 (1 / 100) = 1 / 600.\n\nDenominator:\n(1 / 6) \xB7 (1 / 100) + (1 / 3) \xB7 (3 / 100) + (1 / 2) \xB7 (15 / 100)\n= 1 / 600 + 1 / 100 + 15 / 200\n= [ 1 + 6 + 45 ] / 600 = 52 / 600.\n\n5. Final Probability:\nP(E1 | A) = (1 / 600) / (52 / 600) = 1 / 52.",
    examinerNotes: "Check fractions carefully: leaving common denominator 600 across all terms simplifies the division."
