    modelAnswer: '1. Isometric Exercises (Static):\n- The word "iso" means same, and "metric" means length.\n- In isometric contractions, muscle tension develops against an immovable resistance without any change in the external length of the muscle fibers.\n- No mechanical work is performed (Work = Force \xB7 0 = 0).\n- Examples: Pushing against a solid wall, static plank hold, wall-sit.\n\n2. Isotonic Exercises (Dynamic):\n- The word "iso" means same, and "tonic" means tone/tension.\n- Muscle length changes visibly during contraction, consisting of concentric shortening and eccentric lengthening phases.\n- Mechanical work is performed with joint motion.\n- Examples: Push-ups, pull-ups, bicep curls, squats.',
    examinerNotes: "Must mention that work done is zero in isometric exercises."
